			nickname: 'Topan',
			tagline: 'Efficiency',
			notes:
				'<strong>Goal:</strong> Showcase Anarch "doomrigs" via efficient breakers and Leech.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Gameplan</strong></p>\n\n<p>Topan wants to build their board as quick as possible, taking meat damage in exchange for efficiency. The deck was built with three copies of most cards so that no card is ever lost. <a href="/en/card/30034">Verbal Plasticity</a> is the MVP of this deck as you\'ll want to refill your Grip every so often. <a href="/en/card/35006">Bling</a> adds some much-needed draw but be careful -- if you host a card you can\'t play, it gets trashed!</p>\n\n<p>You want to mulligan for <a href="/en/card/30034">Verbal Plasticity</a> most games, as this allows you to churn through the deck quick. Use Topan\'s ability almost every turn to build your rig as fast as possible. Try to play out your events such as <a href="/en/card/01050">Sure Gamble</a> and <a href="/en/card/35014">Clean Getaway</a> first, then install your Hardware/Resources/Programs after.</p>\n\n<p>The classic Anarch turn currently is draw-draw-install-install. So for Topan, it might look like draw-draw, Sure Gamble, use Topan ability to install one breaker. You might go draw-Topan install-<a href="/en/card/35006">Bling</a>-<a href="/en/card/30020">Creative Commission</a> if you already have <a href="/en/card/35006">Bling</a> on the board.</p>\n\n<p>An early <a href="/en/card/30007">Fermenter</a> is great -- just let it tick up as you build your rig and cash it out later. <a href="/en/card/35007">Gourmand</a> is great to trash accessed expensive ice, or to get rid of <a href="/en/card/30040">Seamless Launch</a> or <a href="/en/card/35043">Nanomanagement</a> in the Core Battle Box matchups.</p>\n\n<p>In all, the deck has multiple copies of most cards so nothing is ever truly lost -- just take damage to build the rig and get running!</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Rig</strong></p>\n\n<p>The endgame rig is 1x <a href="/en/card/30005">Buzzsaw</a>, 1x <a href="/en/card/30025">Echelon</a>, and 1x <a href="/en/card/35009">Rising Tide</a>, with 2x <a href="/en/card/30008">Leech</a>. Extra memory via <a href="/en/card/30031">T400 Memory Diamond</a> should be for <a href="/en/card/30004">Botulus</a>, <a href="/en/card/35007">Gourmand</a>, or <a href="/en/card/30007">Fermenter</a>.</p>\n\n<p>Ideally, you\'d always want a <a href="/en/card/30007">Fermenter</a> ticking up, but this isn\'t feasible at all stages of the game. <a href="/en/card/30004">Botulus</a> is a good way to pressure early, and combined with <a href="/en/card/35007">Gourmand</a>, this allows you to thin the Corp\'s ice as they will overinstall the ice with <a href="/en/card/30004">Botulus</a> on it at times.</p>',
