			name: 'MuslihaT - Core Battle Box',
			nickname: 'MuslihaT',
			tagline: 'Aggression',
			notes:
				'<p><strong>Goal:</strong> Showcase how Crims can exert pressure on the Corp by forcing rezzes at inopportune times to keep their credits low.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Gameplan</strong></p>\n\n<p>MuslihaT wants to hit the ground running with cards like <a href="/en/card/35017">Transfer of Wealth</a> to keep the Corp poor. There\'s a fair bit of "successful run" synergy baked into the deck, which is encouraged by <a href="/en/card/30018">Red Team</a>, such as <a href="/en/card/30015">Carmen</a>, <a href="/en/card/30008">Leech</a>, and <a href="/en/card/30011">Mutual Favor</a>.</p>\n\n<p><a href="/en/card/30018">Red Team</a> can be installed discounted via <a href="/en/card/35022">Open Market</a> -- and remember you can use it three times a turn (one per central), if it\'s feasible.</p>\n\n<p><a href="/en/card/35019">Maglectric Rapid (748 Mod)</a> is a way to force the corp to rez ice they wouldn\'t have rezzed yet, so you can get into other servers. The logic being: they can just let you into HQ if they don\'t have any agendas there. But with <a href="/en/card/35019">Maglectric Rapid (748 Mod)</a>, they now have to reconsider that. But if they rez the HQ ice, you can now run elsewhere!</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Rig</strong></p>\n\n<p>Your endgame rig will look like this: 1x <a href="/en/card/30015">Carmen</a>, 1x <a href="/en/card/35009">Rising Tide</a>, 1x <a href="/en/card/35020">Sang Kancil</a>, and 2x <a href="/en/card/30008">Leech</a>, with a <a href="/en/card/30014">Pennyshaver</a> and <a href="/en/card/30013">Docklands Pass</a> on board. This way, you can discount expensive ice via the <a href="/en/card/30008">Leech</a> counters and keep on running.</p>\n\n<p>The <a href="/en/card/30016">Marjanah</a> are meant to be early game installs if you can\'t find your <a href="/en/card/35009">Rising Tide</a> yet. When you install <a href="/en/card/35009">Rising Tide</a>, you can uninstall Marjanah -- make sure also to discard extra copies to buff <a href="/en/card/35009">Rising Tide</a>\'s strength. You can do this by overdrawing with cards like <a href="/en/card/35026">Ritual</a> and <a href="/en/card/35015">Lie Low</a>.</p>',
